From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: wize-logic <wizelogic@proton.me>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 21:09:17 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] recomp: --rodata-consts writes a float or double read from a
 fixed address in read-only data as a literal

Compilers keep floating-point constants in the XBE's read-only data and read them with an absolute operand (fmul dword ptr [0x1f0a78]). A section the XBE marks neither writable nor code and loads at boot is never written by the title, so the value is known when the function is lifted. On a big-endian host each such read was a byte-reversed load through the stack after the address was formed and mapped; the literal goes to the compiler's constant pool or a register. Only reads of finite values that lie in the section's file bytes are folded (const_load.py); test_const_load.py covers the folded reads, stores, writable data, a NaN and a value past the file bytes.
---
